        end: 197.62,
        startIndex: 23,
        endIndex: 33,
        summary: "美国有 5000 万二十多岁的年轻人，占人口 15%。心理学家、社会学家、神经学家和生育专家早已知道：认领你的二十多岁，是你能为工作、爱情、幸福乃至世界所做的最简单却最具变革性的事。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "50 million 20-somethings", synonyms: ["fifty million twentysomethings", "15 percent of the population"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "claiming your 20s", synonyms: ["take ownership of your twenties", "make the most of your 20s"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "most transformative things you can do", synonyms: ["most life-changing", "biggest impact", "transformative"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 197.77,
        end: 272.98,
        startIndex: 34,
        endIndex: 46,
        summary: "这些是事实：人生 80% 的决定性时刻发生在 35 岁前；职业头十年对收入有指数级影响；超过一半美国人在 30 岁前已找到伴侣；大脑在二十多岁完成最后一次「生长冲刺」；人格在这个时期变化最大；女性生育力在 28 岁达峰。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "80 percent of life's most defining moments", synonyms: ["80% of defining moments", "most defining moments by 35"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "first ten years of a career has an exponential impact", synonyms: ["first decade of career", "exponential impact on income"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "brain caps off its second and last growth spurt", synonyms: ["last growth spurt", "brain rewires for adulthood"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "female fertility peaks at age 28", synonyms: ["fertility peaks at 28", "things get tricky after 35"]),
        ],
