        summary: "格雷格讲了一个故事：当新人的时候，他处理过一起惨烈车祸，训练本能接管了一切，最终把被困女子救了出来。但真正让讲者难忘的是，那次经历之后，格雷格永远无法知道后来发生了什么——消防员很少能得知营救的结果，久而久之，这种缺乏「闭环」会侵蚀士气、加剧倦怠。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "horrific car wreck", synonyms: ["terrible car crash", "awful accident", "horrific crash"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "training took over", synonyms: ["instincts kicked in", "training kicked in", "training took control"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "lack of closure", synonyms: ["no closure", "unresolved outcome", "absence of closure"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 111.05,
        end: 146.46,
        startIndex: 24,
        endIndex: 29,
        summary: "多年后，格雷格成为消防局长，建立了追踪营救结果的系统，让消防员知道自己的努力何时救了一条命、减轻了谁的痛苦。因为他深知：仅仅做重要的工作是不够的，我们需要知道自己的工作有意义、自己是重要的。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "became Fire Chief", synonyms: ["was promoted to chief", "took over as chief", "rose to fire chief"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "tracked the outcomes", synonyms: ["followed the results", "monitored outcomes", "traced the results"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "we matter", synonyms: ["we are important", "we count", "we make a difference"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 146.71,
        end: 192.08,
        startIndex: 30,
        endIndex: 39,
        summary: "过去六年，讲者采访了世界各地成百上千人，问他们「你觉得自己重要吗？」太多人回答「不」：一位医生因保险公司拒绝给病人治疗而无力，一名大学生只在绩点高、体重低时才觉得自己重要，一位老人则因没人再依赖他而觉得自己越来越不重要。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "Do you feel like you matter?", synonyms: ["Do you feel important?", "Do you feel you matter?", "Do you feel valued?"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "denying her patients the care they needed", synonyms: ["refusing patients care", "withholding care", "denying treatment"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "people stop relying on you", synonyms: ["people no longer depend on you", "people stop needing you", "you're no longer needed"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 192.22,
        end: 216.2,
        startIndex: 40,
        endIndex: 46,
        summary: "这些故事和科学研究都表明：要在人生中茁壮成长，我们需要知道自己重要——也就是感到被珍视，并有机会为世界增添价值。当我们觉得自己重要，就会全身心投入、去连接、去参与、去贡献。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "to thrive in life", synonyms: ["to flourish", "to truly live", "to thrive"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "feel valued", synonyms: ["feel appreciated", "feel important", "feel cherished"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "add value", synonyms: ["make a contribution", "contribute", "bring value"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 216.31,
        end: 272.68,
        startIndex: 47,
        endIndex: 56,
        summary: "但当我们被弄得觉得自己不重要，就会退缩：有人转向药物或自残，有人用路怒、网络攻击等愤怒来发泄。随着人工智能淘汰了曾赋予人身份与目标的工作，还会有数百万人面临这场「重要感危机」——摆在我们面前的不只是跟上机器，更是守护「生而为人」的意义。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "lash out in anger", synonyms: ["act out angrily", "erupt in rage", "strike out in anger"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "crisis of mattering", synonyms: ["crisis of significance", "mattering crisis", "crisis of worth"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "what it means to be human", synonyms: ["our humanity", "what makes us human", "human essence"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 272.79,
        end: 313.24,
        startIndex: 57,
        endIndex: 63,
        summary: "我们生活和工作的地方，要么会加剧这场危机，要么成为解决它的关键。讲者参观过威斯康星州菲利普斯的一家工厂，每个工位上都有张卡片，讲述零件如何融入最终产品、附上未来使用者的照片与故事——提醒工人他们不只是在组装零件，而是在建造有意义的东西。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "fuel this crisis", synonyms: ["worsen this crisis", "feed this crisis", "aggravate this crisis"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "a factory in Phillips, Wisconsin", synonyms: ["a plant in Phillips, Wisconsin", "a Wisconsin factory"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "building something meaningful", synonyms: ["creating something meaningful", "making something that matters", "building meaning"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 313.53,
        end: 353.48,
        startIndex: 64,
        endIndex: 70,
        summary: "工作中的「重要感」不是软绵绵的可有可无，而是门好生意：员工知道自己重要，会更努力、更忠诚、更有干劲。想要重要，既需要被珍视，也需要增添价值的机会；讲者总结出公式：去发现世界、社区或邻里中的一个需求，再用你的优势、资源、才华去满足它。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "good business", synonyms: ["smart business", "profitable", "good for the bottom line"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "Identify a need", synonyms: ["spot a need", "find a need", "recognize a need"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "a need in the world or in your community", synonyms: ["a community need", "a real-world need", "an unmet need around you"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 353.54,
        end: 413.0,
        startIndex: 71,
        endIndex: 81,
        summary: "波士顿郊外的朱莉亲身体会到了这一点：母亲去世后，她感到漂泊无依、失去目标，却鼓起勇气向外寻找重新变得重要的路。她发现社区里两类需求——丧亲家庭不知如何处理遗物，另一些家庭因火灾或无家可归需要重建——于是和朋友收集成色尚好的家居用品送给他们，这个简单善举改变了成千上万人的生活，包括她自己。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "full time caregiver", synonyms: ["full-time carer", "round-the-clock caregiver", "primary caregiver"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "unmoored, purposeless", synonyms: ["adrift, without purpose", "lost and aimless", "unmoored and lost"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "two needs in her community", synonyms: ["two community needs", "two unmet needs", "a pair of needs"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 413.11,
        end: 490.26,
        startIndex: 82,
        endIndex: 95,
        summary: "在座的每个人都会经历痛苦的人生转折——失去挚爱、疾病、空巢、退休——它们会动摇我们的「重要感」。但像朱莉一样，我们有机会、甚至有责任让自己重新变得有用，而回归之路可以从一件小事开始：去看看邻居，或当众感谢一位善意的同事。有人可能会想「问题不是我不重要，而是我太重要」，其实这同样是「重要感危机」——真正的重要感是平衡自己与他人的需求。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "painful life transitions", synonyms: ["difficult life changes", "hard transitions", "painful changes"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "make ourselves useful again", synonyms: ["become useful again", "be of use again", "find purpose again"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "checking in on a neighbor", synonyms: ["looking in on a neighbor", "visiting a neighbor", "reaching out to a neighbor"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 490.43,
        end: 568.66,
        startIndex: 96,
        endIndex: 111,
        summary: "梅奥诊所的一项研究测试了简单的韧性干预：让一组同时身为母亲的医疗人员每周碰面一小时、互相支持。三个月后，她们的心理健康显著改善、皮质醇水平下降，还觉得自己成了更好的母亲。这不是孤例——几十年的研究都发现，孩子的韧性根植于身边成年人的韧性，而成年人的韧性根植于人际关系的深度与支持。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "cortisol levels", synonyms: ["stress hormones", "cortisol", "stress hormone levels"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "a child's resilience", synonyms: ["children's resilience", "a kid's resilience", "resilience in children"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "the depth and support of our relationships", synonyms: ["strong relationships", "deep connections", "supportive relationships"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 568.83,
        end: 636.23,
        startIndex: 112,
        endIndex: 122,
        summary: "作为照护者，我们常被叮嘱「先给自己戴上氧气面罩」，但这项研究揭示了更深的东西：朋友才是我们需要的氧气。生命里那一两个、两三个了解我们、看到我们挣扎并会伸手相助的人，才是真正的支持。所以下次犹豫时记住：寻求帮助不是软弱，而是一种慷慨。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "put your oxygen mask on first", synonyms: ["secure your own mask first", "take care of yourself first", "self-care first"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "Friends are the oxygen", synonyms: ["friends are our lifeline", "friends sustain us", "friends are essential"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "asking for help isn't weak", synonyms: ["seeking help is not weakness", "asking for help is strength", "it's okay to ask for help"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 636.35,
        end: 686.81,
        startIndex: 123,
        endIndex: 131,
        summary: "「重要感」非常个人化，但也是关系性的，它能把彼此疏离的世界重新连接。荷兰连锁超市 Jumbo 设立了「慢速收银通道」，收银员花额外时间与老年顾客聊天，这个化解孤独的简单做法已在近 200 家门店推广。启示是：我们不需要建造新空间，只需更用心地对待已有的空间。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "slow checkout lanes", synonyms: ["chat lanes", "slow lanes", "relaxed checkout"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "nearly 200 locations", synonyms: ["almost 200 stores", "about 200 locations", "roughly 200 stores"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "more intentional", synonyms: ["more deliberate", "more purposeful", "more mindful"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 687.03,
        end: 747.76,
        startIndex: 132,
        endIndex: 142,
        summary: "一旦透过「重要感」的镜头看世界，就再也无法视而不见，它甚至成了一种责任，改变了讲者对待家人、朋友、同事乃至陌生人的方式。肯定彼此的价值不仅是正确的事，更是维系健康社会的黏合剂。在成百上千次对话中他学到：内心深处，我们都在寻找同一件事——想知道自己是谁、所做的一切能在世界上产生影响，想知道我们的生命、我们的存在本身是重要的。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "through the lens of mattering", synonyms: ["through the lens of significance", "from the perspective of mattering", "through the mattering lens"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "Affirming each other's worth", synonyms: ["acknowledging each other's value", "valuing one another", "recognizing each other's worth"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "the glue that holds a healthy society together", synonyms: ["what holds society together", "society's binding force", "the bond of a healthy society"]),
        ],
      ),
    ],
  ),
