        end: 59.32,
        startIndex: 0,
        endIndex: 11,
        summary: "讲者回忆初学冥想时，指引很简单：把注意力放在呼吸上，走神就拉回来，可他却在大冬天汗湿了 T 恤、累得精疲力尽。他意识到，即便努力专注，大约一半人迟早会走神做白日梦，或忍不住想刷推特。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "pay attention", synonyms: ["stay focused", "concentrate", "keep your mind on"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "drift off into a daydream", synonyms: ["wander off", "zone out", "lose focus"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "check our Twitter feed", synonyms: ["scroll Twitter", "open social media", "check our phones"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 59.42,
        end: 76.48,
        startIndex: 12,
        endIndex: 16,
        summary: "我们对抗的，是科学已知最古老、最保守的学习过程之一，它可一直回溯到人类最原始的神经系统。这种基于奖赏的学习过程，就叫正强化与负强化。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "evolutionarily conserved learning processes", synonyms: ["ancient learning mechanisms", "primal learning patterns", "hardwired learning"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "positive and negative reinforcement", synonyms: ["reward and punishment", "reinforcement learning", "carrot and stick"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "most basic nervous systems", synonyms: ["primitive nervous systems", "simplest brains", "earliest nervous systems"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 76.62,
        end: 104.0,
        startIndex: 17,
        endIndex: 22,
        summary: "看到诱人的食物，大脑会说「热量、活下去」；尤其是糖会让身体发信号，记住你吃的是什么、在哪儿找到的。于是形成依赖情境的记忆，下次照做：看见食物、吃、爽、再来一次——触发、行为、奖赏。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "calories", synonyms: ["energy", "fuel", "nourishment"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "feel good", synonyms: ["feel great", "get a buzz", "feel satisfied"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "repeat", synonyms: ["do it again", "loop back", "rinse and repeat"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 104.31,
        end: 129.04,
        startIndex: 23,
        endIndex: 28,
        summary: "过了一阵子，我们那富有创造力的大脑想到：这套机制不只能用来记食物在哪儿。下次心情不好，不如吃点好吃的让自己舒服点——于是我们学会生气或难过时吃巧克力、冰淇淋来好受些。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "our creative brains", synonyms: ["our clever minds", "our inventive brains", "our imaginative brains"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "remembering where food is", synonyms: ["locating food", "finding food", "recalling food sources"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "feel better", synonyms: ["feel good", "feel comforted", "lift our mood"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 129.35,
        end: 150.03,
        startIndex: 29,
        endIndex: 33,
        summary: "同一套机制，只是触发条件变了：不再是胃里的饥饿信号，而是「难过」这种情绪信号触发了想吃的冲动。十几岁时，看到校外那些抽烟的叛逆孩子，我们想变酷，于是也开始抽烟。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "different trigger", synonyms: ["new trigger", "changed cue", "another trigger"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "emotional signal", synonyms: ["feeling cue", "mood signal", "emotional cue"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "I want to be cool", synonyms: ["I want to fit in", "I want to look cool", "I want to be liked"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 150.27,
        end: 183.88,
        startIndex: 34,
        endIndex: 40,
        summary: "看见酷、为了变酷而抽烟、感觉良好、再来一次。每重复一次就更熟练，最终变成习惯：一有压力就想抽烟或吃甜食。同样的脑机制，把「学会求生」变成了「用习惯慢慢害死自己」——肥胖和吸烟是全球可预防疾病与死亡的主因。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "smoke to be cool", synonyms: ["smoke to look cool", "smoke to fit in", "smoke for status"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "becomes a habit", synonyms: ["turns into a habit", "becomes automatic", "forms a habit"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "obesity and smoking", synonyms: ["weight and tobacco", "overeating and smoking", "poor diet and nicotine"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 184.19,
        end: 206.92,
        startIndex: 41,
        endIndex: 47,
        summary: "回到呼吸。如果我们不是跟大脑对着干、不是强迫自己专注，而是利用这套天生的奖赏学习机制、再加上一点转折——对当下正在发生的体验真心感到好奇，会怎样？",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "back to my breath", synonyms: ["return to the breath", "back to breathing", "refocus on the breath"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "fighting our brains", synonyms: ["struggling with our minds", "battling our brains", "resisting our minds"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "really curious", synonyms: ["genuinely curious", "truly interested", "deeply curious"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 207.04,
        end: 243.0,
        startIndex: 48,
        endIndex: 59,
        summary: "实验室研究正念训练能否帮人戒烟：多数人此前都试过强迫戒烟，平均失败六次。正念训练不讲「强迫」，只讲「好奇」，甚至让他们去抽——只是抽的时候好好好奇那到底是什么感觉。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "quit smoking", synonyms: ["stop smoking", "give up cigarettes", "kick the habit"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "on average six times", synonyms: ["about six times", "six failed attempts", "six times on average"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "go ahead and smoke", synonyms: ["go ahead, smoke", "feel free to smoke", "go on and smoke"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 243.23,
        end: 278.56,
        startIndex: 60,
        endIndex: 68,
        summary: "一位参与者说：正念抽烟闻着像臭奶酪、尝着像化学药品，呕！她理智上早知道吸烟有害，但带着好奇去觉察才发现烟的味道糟透了。她于是从「知道」走到「体会」，从脑子明白变成骨子里明白，烟的魔咒就此破除，她开始对自己的行为「祛魅」。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "stinky cheese", synonyms: ["smelly cheese", "rotten cheese", "foul cheese"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "from knowledge to wisdom", synonyms: ["from knowing to understanding", "from head to heart", "from intellect to insight"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "knowing it in her bones", synonyms: ["feeling it deeply", "knowing it viscerally", "knowing it in her gut"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 278.85,
        end: 325.96,
        startIndex: 69,
        endIndex: 82,
        summary: "前额叶皮层从进化角度看是大脑最年轻的部分，它在理智上明白我们不该抽烟，会竭尽全力帮我们改变行为、别再吃第二块第三块饼干——这叫认知控制。可惜压力一大，它正是大脑里最先掉线的部分，这时我们就容易对伴侣或孩子发火，明知没用也控制不住。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "prefrontal cortex", synonyms: ["frontal lobe", "executive brain", "reasoning center"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "cognitive control", synonyms: ["self-control", "executive control", "willpower"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "goes offline", synonyms: ["shuts down", "checks out", "stops working"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 326.19,
        end: 389.12,
        startIndex: 83,
        endIndex: 98,
        summary: "前额叶一掉线，我们就退回旧习惯，所以「祛魅」才重要：看清习惯到底给了我们什么，才能更深地理解它、把它刻进骨子里，不必强迫自己克制，因为我们本来就没那么想做了。正念就是清清楚楚看见陷进行为时得到了什么，从身体层面祛魅、自然而然地放手；而它的悖论在于，正念不过是对每时每刻身心正发生的事真正感兴趣、愿意亲近。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "fall back into our old habits", synonyms: ["revert to old habits", "slip into old patterns", "return to old routines"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "letting go", synonyms: ["releasing", "letting it be", "moving on"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "being really interested", synonyms: ["genuinely curious", "truly engaged", "deeply attentive"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 389.3,
        end: 452.12,
        startIndex: 99,
        endIndex: 113,
        summary: "这种愿意转向体验的态度，由天生就有回报的「好奇」支撑。好奇起来，我们会发现渴望不过是一堆身体感觉——发紧、绷着、坐立不安，来了又去；于是走出旧的反应模式，走进「存在」，变成热切等待下一个数据点的内在科学家。一项研究里，正念训练帮人戒烟的效果是金标准疗法的两倍。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "body sensations", synonyms: ["physical sensations", "bodily feelings", "physical feelings"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "step into being", synonyms: ["step into presence", "enter a state of being", "become present"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "inner scientist", synonyms: ["internal observer", "curious investigator", "inner researcher"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "twice as good as gold standard therapy", synonyms: ["twice the gold standard", "double the standard therapy", "twice as effective"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 452.36,
        end: 518.87,
        startIndex: 114,
        endIndex: 127,
        summary: "研究资深冥想者的大脑发现，默认模式网络参与其中。一个假说认为，其中叫后扣带皮层的区域，未必因渴望本身、而是因我们被它卷进去、被带着跑才被激活；当我们放手、带着好奇觉察并走出来，同一脑区就安静下来。如今他们正用那套让我们分心的技术，开发针对核心机制的 App，在最关键的场景把工具送到人们指尖。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "referential processing", synonyms: ["self-referential thinking", "self-referential processing", "default network"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "quiets down", synonyms: ["calms down", "settles down", "goes quiet"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "addictive behaviors", synonyms: ["addictive habits", "compulsive behaviors", "addictions"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
