        startIndex: 172,
        endIndex: 202,
        summary: "孩子每周开一次「圆圈」会议，自己定规则、自己行使权力，包括暂停甚至开除同伴——最后定出的规则和大人物设的几乎一样，但那是他们自己的。学校用 600 块「数字马赛克」覆盖巴西课纲，按兴趣而非年龄分组，孩子自己用 App 给自己的进展打分。课程可以是世界杯，也可以是 45 天组装一辆自行车——而不知道圆周率是 3.1416，车就装不成。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "something we call a circle, which meets once a week", synonyms: ["a weekly circle", "the circle meeting"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "we keep a digital mosaic", synonyms: ["a digital mosaic of learning", "the mosaic tracking system"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "don't have an age category", synonyms: ["mixed-age groups", "no age grouping"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "build a bicycle without knowing that Pi is 3.1416", synonyms: ["build a bike without pi", "assemble a bicycle needing pi"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 779.3,
        end: 919.78,
        startIndex: 203,
        endIndex: 236,
        summary: "讲者说，「回馈社会」这个说法本身就有问题：如果你在回馈，说明你当初拿得太多。50 岁生日前后他在剑桥的奥本山公墓散步，先问「我希望因为什么被记住」，第二圈又问「我到底为什么要被记住」，后者把他带向了别的地方。50 岁那年，他把一本书、上百篇文章和 DVD 全扔进火里：五个孩子从此不必活在他的阴影下，他也从过去的成就里解放出来，可以每次从零开始。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "now is the time to give back", synonyms: ["time to give back", "time to pay it forward"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "you took too much", synonyms: ["you took more than you needed", "you over-took"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "what do I want to be remembered for", synonyms: ["how do I want to be remembered", "what do I want to be known for"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "threw everything I had ever done into that fire", synonyms: ["burned my past work", "burned everything I'd done"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 919.92,
        end: 1053.66,
        startIndex: 237,
        endIndex: 271,
        summary: "他把人生清单称为「空清单」：萨摩亚、马尔代夫、莫桑比克都去过了，喜马拉雅爬过，骆驼走了 59 天到廷巴克图，狗拉雪橇到过磁北极——所以他不觉得自己退休了。他在写新书、两年开了三家公司，还想把这套学校体系免费推向世界，结果发现免费的东西没人要，也许得开始收费。他给所有人的工具很简单：连问三个「为什么」，直到问出「我做这件事是为了什么」。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "my empty bucket list", synonyms: ["a cleared bucket list", "an empty list of things to do"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "nobody wants it for free", synonyms: ["free things get ignored", "no one takes it for free"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "go to the movies on Monday afternoon", synonyms: ["watch a film on a Monday", "take Monday afternoon off"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "asked three ys in a row", synonyms: ["ask why three times", "three whys in a row"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 1053.99,
        end: 1159.38,
        startIndex: 272,
        endIndex: 298,
        summary: "主持人追问：这些想法在商业界早已出现，为什么真正采纳的企业仍然很少？讲者说，确实有大公司零星效仿，比如布兰森放手假期、Netflix 做了一点，但他希望看到的是传教士般的热忱。真正的障碍是「失去控制」的信仰之跃，而几乎没有一个掌权者愿意跳。何况上市公司只有 90 天任期和季报，你说「这个项目不到一代人就能见效」，对方只会让你滚出去。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "these ideas have been out for", synonyms: ["these ideas have existed a while", "ideas around for some time"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "a leap of faith about losing control", synonyms: ["leap of faith on control", "trusting people blindly"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "a company with a 90-day mandate", synonyms: ["90-day mandate", "quarterly accountability"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "get out of here", synonyms: ["get lost", "go away"]),
        ],
      ),
      RetellClip(
        start: 1159.54,
        end: 1301.7,
        startIndex: 299,
        endIndex: 331,
        summary: "谈到教育，讲者认为这是「时机已到的想法」：日本的「塞姆勒主义者」拥有 120 家公司，荷兰有 600 家小公司在这么做，它会自己生长，错一部分也无妨；他真正害怕的是把它变成一套砸钱强推的系统。至于最后一个问题，他回到儿子三岁时的提问「我们为什么存在」——此后所有问题都是它的变体。勇气在于此刻就停下来问「我做这件事是为了什么」，而不是等到临终才后悔没多陪家人。",
        keyPoints: [
          KeyPoint(phrase: "incredibly profound", synonyms: ["deeply profound", "extremely meaningful"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "a dramatic increase in performance", synonyms: ["a big jump in results", "sharply better performance"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "ideas whose time has come", synonyms: ["an idea whose moment has arrived", "a timely idea"]),
          KeyPoint(phrase: "why do we exist", synonyms: ["why are we here", "what are we here for"]),
        ],
      ),
    ],
  ),
